# Portuguese (Brazil) translation for compas-player.
#
# MACHINE DRAFT: pending native review. Tone: short, informal "voce" register
# (imperative in the "voce" form, e.g. "Toque", "Conecte"), Brazilian vocabulary.
#
# Glossary (keep consistent; extend when adding strings):
#   Queue = Fila                    Playlist = Playlist
#   Library = Biblioteca            Settings = Configuracoes
#   Favorites = Favoritos           Most Played = Mais tocadas
#   Shuffle = Aleatorio             Repeat = Repetir
#   Gapless = Gapless (English)     Crossfade = Crossfade (English)
#   Equalizer = Equalizador (EQ)    Plugin = Plugin (Plugin Store = Loja de plugins)
#   Cover / album art = Capa        Metadata = Metadados
#   SD card = Cartao SD             Firmware Update = Atualizacao de firmware
#   On / Off = Ligado / Desligado   Now Playing = Tocando agora
#   Lyrics = Letras                 Books = Livros
#   Stream Media = Streaming        Home = Inicio
#   Track = Faixa                   Song = Musica
#   Kept in English as product or technical names: Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, AirPlay,
#   DLNA, Subsonic, ReplayGain, DAC, USB, ADB, LDAC, aptX, AAC, SBC, PEQ, PIN,
#   Speex, Gateway, Layout, Codec, Bitrate, Play, Power, Weekly Beta, Peaking,
#   Low Shelf, High Shelf. Time zone city names, release labels and codec names
#   are not translated.
# (Accents are used in the actual msgstr values below; this comment block is
#  ASCII only.)
#
